{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles","id":1014470,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants: Cruac Styles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-08T15:11:19-08:00","id":1014470,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants: Cruac Styles","content":"So, I'm looking over the Cruac styles, and their usefulness to me feels vastly different. Where you can almost always use a retainer and give him a task, having stuff grow around you is situationaly good. Randomly changing durability around seems more like something which you'd want in combat, but given the slow speed of casting rituals, it won't happen.<br /> <br /> So can someone give me some reasons why Chaos and Growing is cool besides thematic ? Since from beneficial perspective Void is just better. (Yes, I really wanna be proven wrong here)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:40:33-08:00","id":1014489,"title":"","content":"With Primal Growth your Mandragora Garden is nastier when you animate it for a fight, it becomes much more difficult to get through. You could probably use it to justify expanding the size of your Safe House or Garden. In the connected fiction, at least one vampire was trapped within a cherry tree that grew around it.<br /> <br /> With Unbridled Chaos you can alter those animals that you keep around with Animalism for their swarms, or just enhance your ghouls or retainers, or use it to reinforce a haven that is being attacked or to haven a sanctum you are attacking.<br /> <br /> As an added benefit these things won't act up against you the way your retainer would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:45:40-08:00","id":1014540,"title":"","content":"Unbridled Chaos granting mutations is pretty great. On-tap hurricans are also amazing.<br /> <br /> Primal Growth lets you clone things, potentially en masse. The growth effect is meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:05:14-08:00","id":1014553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1014540#post1014540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On-tap hurricans are also amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially with Cruac having so many weather-based rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The growth effect is meh. </div> </div> </div>It may be a situational one but it really shouldn't be overlooked. It's not as if getting a temporary retainer is that big a deal, at one dot it's the equivalent of a pet with a single trick, and at later dots can still be exceeded by someone you've commanded via your blood or just asked another PC to do, with the added benefit of not being a walking Masquerade breach. Depending on one's fellow PCs, at least.<br /> <br /> Some people might view the thematic use as disposable but it's clear the developer and writers don't, and I don't. Certainly there's a limit, I'm really glad Werewolf got rid of a lot of their exp-tax rites, but these are well within reasonable use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:31:56-08:00","id":1014563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1014540#post1014540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Growth lets you clone things, potentially en masse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure what the use for that would be. Not that it isn't cool, but personally I see more use in the plant growth ability (mainly in conjuction with Mandragora Garden).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T20:09:59-08:00","id":1014586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1014563#post1014563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure what the use for that would be. Not that it isn't cool, but personally I see more use in the plant growth ability (mainly in conjuction with Mandragora Garden).</div> </div> </div> </div>It supercharges things like Animalism 3-5. Otherwise it's nice to terrorize people and getting a large blood supply, since your effective blood supply in the area doubles. Which can, in turn, help with rituals providing you have someone who can suck it out and spill that Vitae and doesn't mind leaving brain damaged wrecks feebly clawing at their faces as they try to understand what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T04:03:25-08:00","id":1015198,"title":"","content":"Primal Growth makes Cruac means of setting oneself up as a fertility god. Not that useful these days, what with the masquerade and not that many people being personally invested in crop cycles, but Cruac wasn't invented for 21st century. It could still be used in the sort of insular communities where Baal-hadad (bull shapeshifters) reside. Or in third world countries where superstitious subsistence farming communities still exist and could be saved from famine this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T04:33:07-08:00","id":1015211,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Cruac Styles, are there new styles other than Primal Growth, Unbridled Chaos, and the Void thing? If not official, than homebrews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T04:40:56-08:00","id":1015214,"title":"","content":"So, Primal Growth = Poison Ivy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T05:50:03-08:00","id":1015227,"title":"","content":"I mean, fertility is useful in todays day and age. The power to make people sized fruit in large number would revolutionize the farming industry.<br /> <br /> It definately has uses, just not for &quot;traditional&quot; PC problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T09:30:38-08:00","id":1015269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1015227#post1015227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, fertility is useful in todays day and age. The power to make people sized fruit in large number would revolutionize the farming industry.<br /> <br /> It definately has uses, just not for &quot;traditional&quot; PC problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>and you can always set up yourself as a strange fertility occultist, who helps couples who have trouble conceiving","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T23:29:00-08:00","id":1017513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1015211#post1015211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Cruac Styles, are there new styles other than Primal Growth, Unbridled Chaos, and the Void thing? If not official, than homebrews?</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent question, I can't afford the book till January.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:16:34-08:00","id":1017658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1015211#post1015211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Cruac Styles, are there new styles other than Primal Growth, Unbridled Chaos, and the Void thing? If not official, than homebrews?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only three in the book, they've been exhibited before. They come with this caveat, 'The following three Styles are the most common exhibited by Cr\u00faac users. Other, rarer kinds exist.'<br /> <br /> There probably are some homebrew, I don't know where they are off-hand but if they've been posted on this board, it's likely you could just do a search.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:31:39-08:00","id":1018045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1015198#post1015198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Growth makes Cruac means of setting oneself up as a fertility god. Not that useful these days, what with the masquerade and not that many people being personally invested in crop cycles, but Cruac wasn't invented for 21st century. It could still be used in the sort of insular communities where Baal-hadad (bull shapeshifters) reside. Or in third world countries where superstitious subsistence farming communities still exist and could be saved from famine this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I can think of lots of ways to use it! Older established couples with money and influence can be made beholden to you because you helped them conceive. Ensure a mistress, or your ghoul running a honey trap on someone you want long term influence over, has a child from a chance encounter. Breed large numbers of disposable animal ghouls. Make my mandragoa garden grow (giant blood sap containing plants)!<br /> <br /> There's plenty you can do with it outside of subsistence farming communities, and out of the styles it's probably less likely to bite you in the ass the way monsters from the void or randomly decaying the building you're standing in might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:25:25-08:00","id":1018253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1014470-secrets-of-the-covenants-cruac-styles?p=1017658#post1017658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only three in the book, they've been exhibited before. They come with this caveat, 'The following three Styles are the most common exhibited by Cr\u00faac users. Other, rarer kinds exist.'<br /> <br /> There probably are some homebrew, I don't know where they are off-hand but if they've been posted on this board, it's likely you could just do a search.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}